@startuml "Bridge - Window (Problem) - Class Diagram"
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<spacer>> transparent
  BorderColor<<spacer>> transparent
  FontColor<<spacer>> transparent
}
hide <<spacer>> stereotype
hide <<spacer>> circle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title Before — the platform is a base class (the problem, GoF p. 151)


abstract class Window {
  + virtual DrawContents(canvas) : void
  + DrawBorder(canvas) : void
  + {abstract} DrawRect(..) : void
  + {abstract} DrawText(..) : void
  + {abstract} Platform : string
}

class XWindow {
  + DrawRect(..) : void
  + DrawText(..) : void
}
class PMWindow {
  + DrawRect(..) : void
  + DrawText(..) : void
}

abstract class IconWindow {
  + DrawContents(canvas) : void
}
class XIconWindow {
  + DrawRect(..) : void
  + DrawText(..) : void
}
class PMIconWindow {
  + DrawRect(..) : void
  + DrawText(..) : void
}

abstract class TransientWindow {
  + DrawContents(canvas) : void
}
class XTransientWindow {
  + DrawRect(..) : void
  + DrawText(..) : void
}
class PMTransientWindow {
  + DrawRect(..) : void
  + DrawText(..) : void
}

Window <|-- TransientWindow
Window <|-- IconWindow
Window <|-- PMWindow
Window <|-- XWindow
IconWindow <|-- PMIconWindow
IconWindow <|-- XIconWindow
TransientWindow <|-- PMTransientWindow
TransientWindow <|-- XTransientWindow

note right of XIconWindow
  Inherits the <i>icon</i> behavior,
  and must <b>copy</b> the X drawing
  code out of XWindow. A class
  cannot inherit from both.
end note

note as N1
  <b>One hierarchy, two reasons to subclass.</b>
  "Icon window" is a kind of window. "X window" is
  also a kind of window. The hierarchy can only
  express one of them, so the leaves are the
  product of the two:

     3 window kinds  x  2 platforms  =  6 classes
     a 3rd platform  ->  9        a 4th kind -> 8

  A test counts the six classes that declare their
  own DrawRect, which is the duplication itself.

  And GoF's second objection (p. 151): the client
  writes `new XIconWindow(..)`, so
  <b>client code becomes platform-dependent</b> — the
  platform is chosen when the code is compiled,
  not when the program runs.
end note

class " " as Spacer1 <<spacer>>
Window -[hidden]- Spacer1
Window -[hidden]- Spacer1
XWindow -[hidden]right- TransientWindow
TransientWindow -[hidden]right- Spacer1
Spacer1 -[hidden]right- IconWindow
IconWindow -[hidden]right- PMWindow
class " " as Spacer2 <<spacer>>
IconWindow -[hidden]- Spacer2
IconWindow -[hidden]- Spacer2
XIconWindow -[hidden]right- Spacer2
Spacer2 -[hidden]right- PMIconWindow
class " " as Spacer3 <<spacer>>
TransientWindow -[hidden]- Spacer3
TransientWindow -[hidden]- Spacer3
XTransientWindow -[hidden]right- Spacer3
Spacer3 -[hidden]right- PMTransientWindow
class " " as Spacer66 <<spacer>>
IconWindow -[hidden]- Spacer66
PMIconWindow -[hidden]right- Spacer66
Spacer66 -[hidden]right- XIconWindow
@enduml
